    "caption": "Craving your favorite banana pudding?\n\nTry making your own version at home and make it a little lighter, too, with help from So Good Almond Milk. Not only is almond milk dairy-free, but it also has a velvety and nutty flavor that will be a great addition to your banana pudding!\n\nMake this dessert for any upcoming special occasions and get all the ingredients you need for this recipe at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour 45 minutes\nYield: 1-2 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n2 cups So Good Almond Milk \n1 tsp. vanilla extract\n3 egg yolks\n½ cup white sugar \n¼ tsp. salt\n2 bananas, sliced \n20 pcs. butter cookies \n¼ cup whipped cream (optional)\n1 tbsp. almonds, chopped\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Combine So Good Almond Milk and vanilla extract in a saucepan, then bring to a simmer. \n2. In a separate heat-proof bowl, whisk together egg yolks, white sugar and salt. Whisk in a small amount of the heated almond milk, then add back the entire mixture into the saucepan. \n3. Continue whisking over low heat until a thick custard forms. Transfer to a bowl, and cover with cling wrap touching the surface of the custard. Chill for 1 hour. \n4. To assemble, layer butter cookies, almond milk custard and bananas in a trifle container. \n5. Top with whipped cream and almonds. \n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
