    "caption": "One thing most of us forget about oatmeal is that it can be used for savory dishes, too!\n\nUsing Quaker Quick-Cook Oatmeal, we created this savory Creamy Mushroom Oatmeal that’s perfect anytime of the day! Not only is it deliciously healthy, but it’s packed with fiber, too.\n\nGet all the ingredients you need for this recipe at #TheMarketplace, and let us know if you enjoyed this recipe in the comments section below!\n\nServing Time: 15 minutes\nYield: 2-3 servings\nOptional: Serve with poached eggs.\n\nIngredients\n\n3 tbsps. olive oil \n½ cup shimeji mushrooms \n½ cup shiitake mushrooms, sliced\n5 cloves garlic, minced\n1 white onion, minced \n½ cup Quaker Quick-Cook Oatmeal\n1 cup vegetable stock \n¼ cup cooking cream \nSalt and pepper to taste\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Heat up olive oil in a pot over medium-high heat. Sear mushrooms until nicely browned, then set aside. \n2. Lower the heat, the sauté garlic and onions until soft. Mix in Quaker Quick-Cook Oatmeal, and toast for 1-2 minutes. \n3. Add in stock and cream, then let simmer for 2 minutes, or until oats are fully cooked. \n4. Season with salt and pepper to taste. \n5. Top each serving with seared mushrooms. \n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
