    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "Australian Festival",
    "caption": "A dish that originated from England, Shepherd’s Pie is a classic dish made with minced meat and topped with mashed potatoes. Different cities in the world have their own versions of it, but one thing we can all agree on is that it pairs so well with a fine glass of red wine.\n\nIf you have a special dinner planned at home, try making this recipe and grabbing a bottle of Grant Burge GB88 Cabernet Sauvignon from #TheMarketplace. Rich with aromas of dark fruit and berries, this is no doubt the perfect pairing to your Shepherd’s Pie. Enjoy!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour 15 minutes\nYield: 4-5 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n3 cups potatoes, peeled and quartered\nSalt and pepper to taste\n4 cloves garlic\n3 tbsps. butter\n¼ cup sour cream\n¼ cup cream cheese, softened\n2 tbsps. olive oil\n½ cup white onions, diced\n½ cup carrots, diced\n500g ground beef\n1 tbsp. tomato paste\n½ tbsp. thyme\n½ cup green peas\n1 tbsp. butter\n1 ½ tbsp. flour\n1 cup Grant Burge GB88 Cabernet Sauvignon\n½ cup beef stock \n2 tbsps. worcestershire sauce\n2 tbsps. flat leaf parsley\n\nProcedure\n\n1. In a pot, boil potatoes in heavily salted water with 3 cloves of garlic. Cook until fork tender, then drain.\n2. In a large bowl, mash potatoes, then mix in butter, sour cream and cream cheese. Season with salt and pepper. Transfer to a piping bag with preferred piping tip. Set aside.\n3. Sauté onion, remaining minced garlic and carrots in olive oil for about 2-3 minutes.\n4. Add in ground beef, and cook until browned. Mix in tomato paste and thyme. Cook until well combined. Add in green peas and butter, then add flour.\n5. Deglaze pan with Grant Burge GB88 Cabernet Sauvignon. Cook for another 2-3 minutes, then mix in beef stock. \n6. Season with worcestershire sauce, salt and pepper.\n7. To assemble, Fill a 4-inch round cutter with cooked ground beef as base. Pipe the mashed potato over ground beef, then slowly remove round cutter.\n8. Torch the mashed potato until nicely toasted and fill the bottom of the plate with sauce. Garnish with parsley. \n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
