    "category": "RECIPE",
    "categorySource": "inferred",
    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "Australian Festival",
    "caption": "To warm up those cold, chilly days, whip up this Tomato Ricotta Risotto made with Woolworths Australian Diced Tomatoes.\n\nPremium, juicy, and bursting with flavor, these tomatoes go so well with rich, creamy ricotta. White wine and garlic cut through the richness of the risotto, making this recipe one to bookmark if the craving for something rich, creamy, and tangy hits. Find Woolworths products exclusively at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 40-45 minutes\nYield: 2-3 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n4 cups chicken stock\n2 tbsps. olive oil \n1 cup onion, diced\n2 cloves garlic, minced\n1 ½ cups arborio rice\n1 tbsp. tomato paste\n1 tbsp. Italian seasoning\n½ cup white wine\n2 cans Woolworths Australian Diced Tomatoes \n½ cup white wine\n⅓ cup parmesan cheese\n2 tbsps. Butter\nSalt and pepper to taste\n1 cup ricotta cheese\n⅓ cup cherry tomatoes, halved\n2 tbsps. annatto oil\n2 tbsps. basil leaves\n\nProcedure\n\n1. In a pot over medium low heat, add in chicken stock and let simmer.\n2. Set a skillet over medium heat, then add in olive oil, onions and garlic. Sauté until fragrant and tender.\n3. Mix in arborio rice. Add tomato paste and italian seasoning, then cook until the color has darkened.\n4. Deglaze pan with white wine, then mix in Woolworths Australian Diced Tomatoes. \n5. Slowly add in one cup of chicken stock while constantly stirring. Once absorbed, add the remaining stock cup by cup.\n6. Cook for 20-25 minutes while frequently stirring. Once cooked, add in parmesan cheese and butter. Season with salt and pepper. \n7. Top risotto with ricotta, cherry tomatoes, a drizzle of annatto oil, and garnish with basil leaves.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
