    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "Australian Festival",
    "caption": "Steak au poivre is a classic French dish where steak, traditionally a filet mignon, is coated in peppercorns that form a crust around the meat when cooked.\n\nOur version uses porterhouse, specifically Aussie Fresh Porterhouse, which is juicy, meaty, and full of flavor. Follow the instructions on how to prepare it below and pair it with your favorite soup, salad, or sides. Make this on a special evening for a dinner to remember.\n\nFind Aussie Fresh Porterhouse at #TheMarketplace, along with other fresh and premium meats!\n\nServing Time: 25-30 minutes\nYield: 2-3 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n1 slab Aussie Fresh Porterhouse\n4 tbsps. black pepper, coarsely ground\n1 tbsp. salt\n2 tbsps. olive oil\n1 tbsp. butter\n1 tbsp. flour\n1 cup beef stock\n1 tbsp. worcestershire sauce\n1 cup mixed greens\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Pat dry Aussie Fresh Porterhouse. Season with 3 tbsps. black pepper and salt.\n2. Set a cast iron skillet over high heat. Once smoking, add in olive oil, and sear steak on both sides. Cook until the internal temperature reaches 135°C-140°C. Set aside, and let rest for 8 minutes.\n3. Using the same pan over low heat, add in butter and flour. Whisk in beef stock until it thickens. Season with worcestershire sauce and the remaining black pepper.\n4. Serve Porterhouse with sauce and mixed greens.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
