    "caption": "Nothing beats a comforting plate of Beef Stroganoff, especially if it’s made with premium MV Margaret River Wagyu Beef Cubes.\n\nTraditionally from Russian origin, beef stroganoff combines Worcestershire sauce and sour cream for a tangy, meaty sauce that goes well with fettuccine (or your choice of pasta or noodles). This is a great comfort dish that can be enjoyed any day of the week. Find MV Margaret River Wagyu Beef Cubes, along with other premium beef cuts, at #TheMarketplace where you can always trust that the meats are fresh.\n\nServing Time: 40-45 minutes\nYield: 2-3 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n500g MV Margaret River Wagyu Beef Cubes\n2 tbsps. olive oil\n2 tbsps. butter\n1 cup onion, diced\n2 cloves garlic, minced\n1 cup mushroom, sliced\n½ tsp. paprika\n2 tbsps. flour \n2 ½ cups beef stock \n2 tbsps. dijon mustard\n1 tbsp. worcestershire\n¾ cup sour cream\n400g fettuccine, cooked according to package instructions\n⅛ cup parsley, chopped\n⅛ cup parmesan cheese\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Pat dry MV Margaret River Wagyu Beef Cubes, then season with salt and pepper. Sear Wagyu Cubes in olive oil over high heat. Set aside.\n2. Using the same pan on medium heat, add in butter, then sautè onion and garlic until tender. Add in mushrooms, and cook until nicely browned.\n3. Mix in paprika, flour, beef stock, dijon mustard and worcestershire sauce. Whisk until smooth and thickened. \n4. Transfer back seared beef cubes, then season with salt and pepper. Turn off heat, then mix in sour cream. \n5. Serve over cooked fettuccine, and garnish with parmesan cheese and parsley.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
